WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.944
Bot traffic reporting is a separate feature from core analytics.

00:00:03.944 --> 00:00:08.940
The owner grants it to an account only after verifying its plan payment.

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:17.781
An administrator can see the setup screen; a customer without active access should not be able to create or view a bot report.

00:00:17.981 --> 00:00:24.981
For an authorized site, create its bot token and copy it once into that site's server environment.

00:00:24.981 --> 00:00:29.921
The token must never appear in frontend code or the public page.

00:00:29.921 --> 00:00:34.862
If it is exposed, rotate it immediately and update your server middleware.

00:00:35.062 --> 00:00:40.125
Server middleware can send recognized crawler requests to the bot endpoint.

00:00:40.125 --> 00:00:43.347
Browser visitors are not counted as bots.

00:00:43.347 --> 00:00:51.170
The report describes observed requests, not an endorsement or proof that an AI system used your content.

00:00:51.170 --> 00:00:55.773
Check verification status and the event time before drawing conclusions.
